{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Crisis at the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Calling Tech Support"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Will and Won't in the if-clause to Express Refusal or Strong Disapproval"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the first conditional to talk about possibilities in the present or future - things which might happen. <br>You use the if clause with <span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> to express refusal or disapproval."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A first conditional sentence consists of two clauses, an \"if\" clause and a main clause: <br><br> <span class=\"italic\">If you won't be here for your team, then we'll have a big problem.</span>  <br>= The possibility of not being here will be met with strong disapproval. <br><br> Look at the chart for an example of refusal and disapproval:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Refusal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It won't do us any good if we won't find a middle ground.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disapproval\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you won't pull yourself together in front of them, it will show them a bad example.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you won't be here, you'll have to talk with me later.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It won't do us any good if we're not on the same page. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Perfect Infinitives to Talk About Future Action"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Perfect Infinitive to talk about an action that will be completed at a point in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Perfect Infinitive can refer to an action that will be completed, or that is expected to be completed at some point in the future. <br><br> You use the Perfect Infinitive to talk about future actions with verbs like <span class=\"italic\">expect, pretend, prefer</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">hope</span>. <br><br> Structure: <br>verb + to have + past participle. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I hope to have wrapped up the agenda by 10."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I prefer the fridges to have been checked both morning and night for supplies."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I hope to have resolved our fridge problem."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I expect all of you to have come in for four o'clock to prepare for dinner. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "customer relations "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the process and manner in which a business develops, establishes and maintains relationships with its customers "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Concerning customer relations, you've all been working hard. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about customer relations."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "non-verbal communication"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "communication without the use of spoken language"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're getting better with non-verbal communication ... smiling more, most of you. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "R and R"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "rest and relaxation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So you have the morning off tomorrow so I hope you get some R and R.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have a word with someone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to speak privately "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rachel, I'd like to have a word with you.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "presumptions"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "acts of assuming something to be true  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want to make any presumptions, but I feel like something's going on with you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pompous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling or \u200bshowing that you \u200bthink you are \u200bbetter or more \u200bimportant than other \u200bpeople "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't stand how pompous the customers are. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cultural bias"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of interpreting and judging phenomena by standards inherent to one's own culture "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A lot of them have a cultural bias towards me.   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Why on earth ... ?"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to show surprise or shock when asking \u201cwhy\u201d  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why on earth did you take your shoes and socks off in the dining room?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a memo to employees about problems with customer service."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about what will have happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my memo aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to feedback from friends."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of five errors service people make when they deal with customers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a memo (150 words minimum) to a restaurant staff highlighting the mistakes they've made and say how they can improve their customer service. (use <span class=\"it